      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The latest guard addresses column-zero braces by counting them, but heredoc content can satisfy that count while still truncating the secret scan and allowing an opaque credential to reach an output.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 423,
          "message": "The block-count check can be balanced by Terraform block-like text inside a heredoc, leaving a credential-bearing local and output undetected.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The new assertion compares counts of column-zero closing braces and top-level block headers. It does not distinguish real Terraform syntax from heredoc content. The output and locals scan at line 428 stops at the first column-zero closing brace.",
            "failureScenario": "A locals heredoc can contain a line such as `resource \"example\" {` followed by a column-zero `}` before a later local assignment that references a storage access key. Those heredoc lines add one matching block header and closing brace, so this count assertion still passes. The scan then truncates the locals block before the credential assignment; an output referencing that local can pass because its evaluated key is opaque. AC RELEASE-ID-04 is not enforced for this case (OWASP A02:2025 Security Misconfiguration)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
